.TH FERRONOTE 1 "August 2026" "ferronote 1.2.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ferronote \- a blazing-fast terminal note-taking app inspired by Notational Velocity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ferronote
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBferronote\fR is a Rust TUI application that brings the modeless search-first philosophy of Notational Velocity to the terminal.
Searching and note creation are unified into a single input bar.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dir\fR \fIPATH\fR
Specify custom notes directory (default: ~/.ferronotes/ or config location).
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-import\fR \fIPATH\fR
Import notes from a file (.md/.txt), a directory, or a .zip archive.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-export\fR \fIPATH\fR
Export full vault to a .zip archive or a single note to an HTML file.
.TP
\fB\-\-trash\fR
List soft-deleted notes currently in the trash.
.TP
\fB\-\-restore\fR \fIFILENAME\fR
Restore a soft-deleted note from the trash by filename.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help information.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
\fB/\fR or \fBCtrl+L\fR
Focus search bar.
.TP
\fBCtrl+N\fR
Clear search bar and start a new note.
.TP
\fBTab / Shift+Tab / Esc\fR
Cycle focus between Search Bar, Note List, and Editor.
.TP
\fBEnter\fR
Open selected note / Create note / Follow [[Wiki-Link]].
.TP
\fBCtrl+S\fR
Force save current note.
.TP
\fBCtrl+D\fR
Soft delete selected note from the Search bar or Note List (prompts for y/n).
In the editor's View mode, scrolls half a page down instead.
.TP
\fBCtrl+P\fR
Toggle Interactive Settings Overlay.
.TP
\fBCtrl+V\fR
Toggle About Overlay.
.TP
\fBMouse Drag\fR
Drag panel divider line to resize notes list and content panel (20%-40%).
.TP
\fB?\fR
Toggle Help Overlay.
.TP
\fBCtrl+Q\fR
Quit application.
.SH VIM MODE
The built-in editor opens notes in a Vim-style View mode supporting motions
(\fBh j k l w b e f t\fR ...), operators (\fBdd dw diw cw ciw cc yy yiw D C Y\fR),
\fBr\fR (replace), \fBJ\fR (join), visual selections (\fBv\fR / \fBV\fR),
in-editor regex search (\fB/\fR, \fBn\fR, \fBN\fR), and half/full page
scrolling (\fBCtrl+D\fR / \fBCtrl+U\fR / \fBCtrl+F\fR).
Press \fBi\fR, \fBa\fR, or \fBo\fR to enter Insert mode and \fBEsc\fR to
return to View mode. See the online keybindings reference for the full table.
